    "created_at": "2022-02-03T17:20:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-03T17:20:22Z",
    "body": "`this` has [special meaning](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/functions.html#declaring-this-in-a-function) in typescript.\r\n\r\nadditionally, oninputreport is a property and not a method. you'd probably want to do `MySubclass: ctor { this.addEventListener('inputreport', this._onInputReport.bind(this)) }`",
